Bat Fur Quest	25	{"kind":"quest","title":"Bat Fur Quest","wikiPath":"/Bat_Fur_Quest","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"South Qeynos","detail":"Start zone"},{"kind":"quest","where":"Caleah Herblender","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[],"rewards":[{"text":"Faction, Experience, Coin"}],"card":{"title":"Bat Fur Quest","lines":["Minimum Level: 2","Classes: All","Related Zones: None","Related NPCs: newbie mobs, Drawna Opimsor"]},"links":["Qeynos","Caleah Herblender","Drawna Opimsor","Faction","Bat Fur","Rat Whiskers","Fire beetle eye","Order of Three","Bloodsabers","Guards of Qeynos","Opal Dark Briar"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Caleah Herblender","text":"Drawna. Are we all out of Bat Fur again?"},{"npc":"Caleah Herblender","text":"Hmm. Let's see if we can find someone to help replenish our stock of Rat Whiskers and Bat Fur. I need these items for a new little experiment I'm working on."},{"npc":"Caleah Herblender","text":"Greetings, and welcome to my humble little shop. I sell and trade various goods for my fellow wizards of the Order of Three. My assistants, Hanlore and Drawna, specialize in magicians' and enchanters' goods and would be glad to help you, too."},{"npc":"Caleah Herblender","text":"I need someone to gather up the three ingredients for a new spell I'm working on. I need some [rat whiskers], a [fire beetle eye], and a patch of [bat fur]. Thanks for helping me, young ______."},{"npc":"Caleah Herblender","text":"I need someone to gather up the three ingredients for a new spell I'm working on. I need some [rat whiskers], a [fire beetle eye], and a patch of [bat fur]. Thanks for helping me, young ______."},{"npc":"Caleah Herblender","text":"I need someone to gather up the three ingredients for a new spell I'm working on. I need some [rat whiskers], a [fire beetle eye], and a patch of [bat fur]. Thanks for helping me, young ______."},{"npc":"Caleah Herblender","text":"All right. Remember, I need all three ingredients to test this spell out. Keep up the good work, ______."},{"npc":"Caleah Herblender","text":"All right. Remember, I need all three ingredients to test this spell out. Keep up the good work, ______."},{"npc":"Caleah Herblender","text":"Hmm. Good job, ______, let's give this a try. Flame and fire. Heat and spark. Touch of Ro, light this dark! Ahh. It stills needs a little work, I guess. Thanks for your help, here's a little something for your effort."},{"npc":"Drawna Opimsor","text":"Yeah, it seems hard to come by lately. We're all out of Rat Whiskers, too."}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T08:52:17.649Z","outOfEra":false}
Crusader's Tests#Crusader's Test of the Lord (#7)	25	{"kind":"quest","title":"Crusader's Tests","wikiPath":"/Crusader's_Tests","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"East Cabilis","detail":"Start zone"},{"kind":"quest","where":"Arch Duke Xog, Lord Gikzic, Lord Korzin, Lord Qyzar","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[{"name":"Greenmist Design Pattern","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Greenmist_Design_Pattern"},{"name":"Chunk of Tynnonium","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Chunk_of_Tynnonium"},{"name":"Hammer of 1406","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Hammer_of_1406"},{"name":"Notes from the Greenmist Tome","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Notes_from_the_Greenmist_Tome"},{"name":"Greenish Metal Shard","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Greenish_Metal_Shard"},{"name":"Greenmist Khukri Blade","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Greenmist_Khukri_Blade"},{"name":"Bone Chips (Quest)","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Bone_Chips_(Quest)"},{"name":"Sarnak Whelp Head","qty":4,"wikiPath":"/Sarnak_Whelp_Head"},{"name":"Page of a Tome","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Page_of_a_Tome"},{"name":"Tome Binder","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Tome_Binder"},{"name":"Magically Locked Tome","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Magically_Locked_Tome"},{"name":"Glowing Skull","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Glowing_Skull"},{"name":"Shovel","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Shovel"},{"name":"Chalp Diagram","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Chalp_Diagram"},{"name":"Charasis Tome","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Charasis_Tome"},{"name":"Charasis Tome Copy","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Charasis_Tome_Copy"},{"name":"Droga Jail","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Droga_Jail"},{"name":"The History of the Greenmist","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/The_History_of_the_Greenmist"},{"name":"Mirror of Self-loathing","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Mirror_of_Self-loathing"}],"rewards":[{"text":"Pawn's Khukri","item":"Pawn's Khukri","wikiPath":"/Pawn%27s_Khukri"},{"text":"Knave's Khukri","item":"Knave's Khukri","wikiPath":"/Knave%27s_Khukri"},{"text":"Squire's Khukri","item":"Squire's Khukri","wikiPath":"/Squire%27s_Khukri"},{"text":"Knight's Khukri","item":"Knight's Khukri","wikiPath":"/Knight%27s_Khukri"},{"text":"Zealot's Khukri","item":"Zealot's Khukri","wikiPath":"/Zealot%27s_Khukri"},{"text":"Crusader's Khukri","item":"Crusader's Khukri","wikiPath":"/Crusader%27s_Khukri"},{"text":"Hero's Khukri","item":"Hero's Khukri","wikiPath":"/Hero%27s_Khukri"},{"text":"Lord of Pain's Khukri","item":"Lord of Pain's Khukri","wikiPath":"/Lord_of_Pain%27s_Khukri"},{"text":"Greenmist","item":"Greenmist","wikiPath":"/Greenmist"}],"card":{"title":"Crusader's Tests","lines":["Minimum Level: 1+","Classes: Shadow Knight","Faction: Crusaders of Greenmist (amiable?)"]},"links":["Cabilis","Arch Duke Xog","Lord Gikzic","Lord Korzin","Lord Qyzar","Shadow Knight","Crusaders of Greenmist","Pawn's Khukri","Knave's Khukri","Squire's Khukri","Knight's Khukri","Zealot's Khukri","Crusader's Khukri","Hero's Khukri","Enduring Breath","Lord of Pain's Khukri","Greenmist","Shissar","Greenmist (Spell)","Sarnak Whelp Head","A Sarnak Hatchling","Lake of Ill Omen","Page of a Tome","Froglok Raider","Swamp of No Hope","Tome Binder","Magically Locked Tome","Glowing Skull","Greater Scalebone","Lesser Charbone Skeleton","Lesser Icebone Skeleton","Kurn's Tower","An iksar knight","Warsliks Wood","A Forest Giant Sapling","Misscribed Gate","Misscribed Lifetap","Scroll in a Bottle","Shovel","Chalp Diagram","An Iksar crusader","Coin","Tracker Azeal","Firiona Vie","Hero Goxnok","A drachnid spy","Charasis Tome","Charasis Tome Copy","Visceral Dagger","The Visceral Dagger","Failed crypt raider","Kaesora","Spectral Courier","City of Mist","A dark librarian","Castle Mistmoore","A dark ass`t librarian","A goblin penkeeper","A goblin penmaster","Droga Jail","Frontier Mountains","A Bone Key","A Bone Necklace","A Stone Key","An enslaved iksar","Coarse Iron Needle","Stupendous Tome","Librarian Zimor","Loremaster Piza`tak","Grand Lorekeeper Kino Shai`din","The History of the Greenmist","Note to Oxyn","Hierophant Oxyn","Bottle of Liquid Deklium","Alchemist Granika","The Overthere","A Glowing Cliff Golem","Chunk of Tynnonium","Note to Librarian Zimor","Notes from the Greenmist Tome","Weaponsmith Ko`Zirr","Hammer of 1406","A Alchemist`s Acolyte","Greenish Metal Shard","Rile's Shattered Blade","Karnor's Castle","Drusella Sathir","Howling Stones","Mirror of Self-loathing","A tormented tradesman","Cracked Mirror of Self-Loathing","Haggle Baron Dalnir","Greenmist Design Pattern","Greenmist Khukri Blade","The Penance","Crusaders Of Greenmist","Legion of Cabilis","Sarnak Head Pack","Full Pack of Sarnak Heads","Froglok raider","A forest giant","Dalnir","Brood of Kotiz","Scaled Mystics","An Apprentice Herbalist","Bone Chips (Quest)"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Arch Duke Xog","text":"Welcome into our brotherhood. Know you that our way is the way of pain. Do as we say and you shall climb the rungs of knighthood. Listen well to the Lords of Pain within this temple and follow the words of the hierophants, for Cazic-Thule speaks to us through them. Take this khukri. It is the chosen weapon of the Crusaders and can deliver great pain unto our foes. Go now and learn our ways. Seek out Lord Gikzic."},{"npc":"Lord Gikzic","text":"You dare to intrude upon the presence of a Lord of Pain?! Such foolish acts can only be those of a knight in training. Are you a [knight in training]?"},{"npc":"Lord Gikzic","text":"If you are a pawn, then let us begin with a simple test. Complete the test and you shall be rewarded with a new khukri. Do you [wish to perform the test of a pawn]?"},{"npc":"Lord Gikzic","text":"You shall carry this pack. Within it you shall combine 4 sarnak hatchling heads. When you have the full sarnak head pack then you shall return it to me along with your pawn's khukri and I shall reward you with the khukri of a knave. Beware, the sarnak are our most hated foes and even their whelps are quite formidable fighters. Be sure to seek out Klok Mugruk. He may have some curscale armor available."},{"npc":"Lord Gikzic","text":"You have learned to behead your opponents with great precision. Take the khukri of the knave. It shall prove most formidable in combat when wielded by a young crusader. You may now assist us with a [greater concern] than your training."},{"npc":"Lord Gikzic","text":"A tome has been taken from us. An expeditionary unit was returning to Cabilis when they were overtaken by a band of froglok raiders. The odds were greatly in their favor, but our forces would soon cut them down. Then, as abruptly as the battle began, it came to an end. The frogs retreated. The only item they took was an ancient tome entitled 'The Origins of Pain'. What the frogs want with it is unknown to us. Will you [retrieve the tome]?"},{"npc":"Lord Gikzic","text":"The tome ripped open in battle. There were but ten pages. This is one of those pages. You must find the remainder and the tome binder. Place the pages within the binder and once you combine them, the binder shall magically lock. Do not look upon the pages, for the words would bring a great madness upon you. Your task is simply to seek out the froglok raiders and return the magically locked tome to me. Return it with a knave's khukri and I shall give you a more powerful weapon."},{"npc":"Lord Gikzic","text":"You have done as instructed. You are wise to hand this tome to me. It could bring you nothing more than insanity. As your reward, you shall have the squire's khukri. Soon you shall wield the knight's khukri, but that is for another Lord of Pain to decide."},{"npc":"Lord Korzin","text":"What is it you seek? Eternal suffering?"},{"npc":"Lord Korzin","text":"Then follow the words of Cazic-Thule and may his blessed curses rain upon your soul as they shall on all of his faithful servants. Were you [sent] to me by Gikzic?"},{"npc":"Lord Korzin","text":"You were sent to me. You must be the squire who found the ancient tome, 'The Origins of Pain'. I can use a talented crusader such as yourself. In my dreams, Cazic-Thule has spoken to me. He instructed me to seek out the 'Skull of Torture' which was last reported to be within the torture tower of the ancient Lord of Pain, Kurn. Will you [accept the calling]?."},{"npc":"Lord Korzin","text":"As if you had a choice. Seek out the tower of Kurn and find the Skull of Torture. You should be able to easily recognize this skull as it glows with the power of Cazic Thule. Return it to me with your squire's khukri and I shall reward you with the knight's khukri. Go at once."},{"npc":"Lord Korzin","text":"Excellent work! You are no squire. You are now a knight of the crusaders. Your next step shall be zealot. And every zealot wields a magical khukri."},{"npc":"Lord Qyzar","text":"You are a student of our ways? I would hope so. I seek a knight in search of a way to prove his allegiance and a way to earn his [zealot khukri]."},{"npc":"Lord Qyzar","text":"In search of a zealot khukri? I have heard much of your deeds to aid us. I offer it to you in exchange for your service. I have dispatched a knight named Grizzle to seek out the Kromdul fortress called Chalp. He was to secretly map Chalp and return with a [Chalp diagram]. He has yet to return. Perhaps you can [rescue Grizzle]."},{"npc":"Lord Qyzar","text":"If you can find the knight in Chalp and have him hand you the Chalp diagram, you shall become a zealot and wield a zealot khukri. All I need are the Chalp diagram and your knight khukri."},{"npc":"Lord Qyzar","text":"At last!! The Chalp diagram. I shall see that the emperor gets this at once. You have proven yourself more than just a mere knight, you are a zealot. Being new to the temple we have need of you in a [matter of betrayal]."},{"npc":"Lord Qyzar","text":"One of our agents, a hero by the name of Goxnok, has found evidence that the book entitled 'Charasis' has been taken from this temple and is to be delivered to an unknown foe in the Outlands. Go at once to the lower levels of the temple and greet Goxnok. Hurry, before he departs!"},{"npc":"an Iksar crusader","text":"The Charasis Tome, the tome of the old city of Charasis. It was taken from this temple and must be returned. The one sent to [apprehend the traitor] who stole the tome must be [ready to depart] with me at once."},{"npc":"an Iksar crusader","text":"I am afraid I do not know. The babble is that he is from Cabilis, but he could have been a disguised sarnak. Who knows? The tink is that at night within the Outland territory, near the old skinless outpost, they are to meet. We should depart at once. Go get outfitted and let me know when you are [ready to depart]."},{"npc":"an Iksar crusader","text":"As I have reported, the babble states they appear to be skinless stubs who ride giant spiders. Most encounters occur when the moon is high. Little is known about them and only in recent weeks have they begun to appear."},{"npc":"Tracker Azeal","text":"I'm going to start my patrol. I'll report back by morning."},{"npc":"Hero Goxnok","text":"The Charasis Tome has been scribed and now another copy exists. The traitor obviously wants to keep a copy for himself. I am told you will deliver both copies to Lord Qyzar along with your zealot khukri and you shall be awarded that of a crusader. Let us rest for a minute and then I shall show you the meeting place."},{"npc":"Hero Goxnok","text":"Come along. If we get separated, look for the humanoid wolf camp and beyond the tunnel, you shall find the meeting place of the spider riders and the traitor."},{"npc":"Hero Goxnok looks over at you and sizes you up before continuing on. He","text":"We should continue, follow me."},{"npc":"Hero Goxnok sighs slowly, seeing the confusion on your face. He","text":"Yes, ______, I am the traitor. What I can gain by giving up this tome outweighs any patriotic obligations I may have once had. That city is dead, it is now time for us to grasp at our own destinies. I now give you two choices, Iksar. You can walk away and never speak of this to anyone......or you can die. What will it be?"},{"npc":"Hero Goxnok","text":"Die by the power of Greenmist!!"},{"npc":"Hero Goxnok's corpse","text":"You shall now be a wanted man.. The Union of Vie shall punish you."},{"npc":"Lord Qyzar","text":"Congratulations! You are now a true crusader, but there is no time for celebration. We have lost two of our operatives. Crusaders Golin and Fodcod were dispatched to seek out an ancient artifact, the [visceral dagger]. Where they have gone, I do not know. They have been gone far too long. Find them and return the dagger to me with your crusader khukri and you shall be a hero."},{"npc":"Lord Qyzar","text":"The visceral dagger was an ancient torturing weapon. I do not know much of it other than that it was forged by a member of the Brood of Kotiz, but that was ages ago. He is surely dust by now."},{"npc":"Arch Duke Xog","text":"Once a Lord of Pain, Argest is now a great explorer. No lizard has seen more of Kunark than he. He returned one season ago to tell tales of an [ancient library]. He said that he believed that there he would find a tome which would reveal the location of the ancient crusader weapon, Greenmist."},{"npc":"Arch Duke Xog","text":"There are many ancient libraries yet to be discovered. Our once great cities have been decimated, if not by our foes, then by nature itself. Within the outlands are many ruins which have yet to reveal themselves. We look forward to the discovery of these ruins by such explorers as Lord [Argest] the Great."},{"npc":"an enslaved iksar","text":"Forget them. I believe all six scrolls lie in the [Kaesora Library] and that is no safe place for any explorer. The scrolls are not readable by any living person, but I came here in search of a machine which may be able to decipher them, the [Stupendous Contraption]. Should you return to Cabilis, see that the Arch Duke hears of the scrolls."},{"npc":"an enslaved iksar","text":"I have learned it was a machine tinkered by a legendary gnome. It has many uses. It lies in the slave pens of Droga. Perhaps it may be used to decipher the [Scrolls of Vok Na Zov]. I have leearned that it will not work without a [contraption needle]. Luckily I have found one in my journeys."},{"npc":"an enslaved iksar","text":"The contraption needle is a piece of the machine, the [Stupendous Contraption]. It won't operate without it and if you want it, you're going to have to bring me the [pen keys]."},{"npc":"an enslaved iksar","text":"Pen keys!! I need the pen keys to get out of here! Find the ones who hold these keys. Bring me the key to pen number 1 and both keys to the pen gates. Do so and I shall give you the [contraption needle]."},{"npc":"Arch Duke Xog","text":"A legible tome of the scrolls of Vok Na Zov! What a find this is!! May the unholy curses of Cazic flow through you. Please accept the weapon of a Lord of Pain. To abandon it is to abandon our ways and earn yourself the hatred of our order."},{"npc":"a drachnid spy","text":"You shall not take the tome from me!! I shall snack upon your blood-drained corpse."}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T09:39:49.598Z","outOfEra":true}
The Bread Shipment (Halas)	25	{"kind":"quest","title":"The Bread Shipment (Halas)","wikiPath":"/The_Bread_Shipment_(Halas)","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"Halas","detail":"Start zone"},{"kind":"quest","where":"Hetie McDonald","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[{"name":"Bag of Bread Loaves","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Bag_of_Bread_Loaves"}],"rewards":[{"text":"Faction, Experience, Coin"}],"card":{"title":"The Bread Shipment (Halas)","lines":["Minimum Level: 1","Classes: All","Related Zones: Southern Karana","Related NPCs: Jarlen Meadowgreen"]},"links":["Halas","Hetie McDonald","Southern Karana","Jarlen Meadowgreen","Muffin Quests","Bag of Bread Loaves","Runnyeye","Merchants of Halas","Wolves of the North","Shamen of Justice"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Hetie McDonald","text":"Hello there, Zokkor. I'm afraid times are getting tough. The plague has hindered our ability to restock food, and I am finding myself running short on baked goods lately. Would you be [willing to help] me out?"},{"npc":"Hetie McDonald","text":"Excellent! There are two ways you can help me. If you [can bake] you can make me some muffins so I don't run out. Or you [can travel] a ways for me and pick up some bread."},{"npc":"Hetie McDonald","text":"Good! Now there is a man who lives in the plains to the south. He goes by Jarlen Meadowgreen. He is a respected baker and makes some good quality bread. Just let him know that you want a bag of bread loaves."},{"npc":"Hetie McDonald","text":"Fresh bread! Thank you so much, I will put this on the shelves straightaway. Here is your payment as promised."},{"npc":"Jarlen Meadowgreen","text":"So, ya want some of my bread is that it? Well, you've come to the right place I'd say. My brothers told me the market was ripe for that sort of thing so I decided to move on over here. Anyway, hand over two gold pieces and I'll give ya a sack of bread made by me own two hands."}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T09:54:16.794Z","outOfEra":false}
Bone Chips Felwithe	25	{"kind":"quest","title":"Bone Chips Felwithe","wikiPath":"/Bone_Chips_Felwithe","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"Northern Felwithe","detail":"Start zone"},{"kind":"quest","where":"Yeolarn Bronzeleaf","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[{"name":"Bone Chips","qty":4,"wikiPath":"/Bone_Chips"}],"rewards":[{"text":"Spell: Strike","item":"Strike","wikiPath":"/Strike"},{"text":"Fine Steel Short Sword","item":"Fine Steel Short Sword","wikiPath":"/Fine_Steel_Short_Sword"}],"card":{"title":"Bone Chips Felwithe","lines":["Minimum Level: 1","Classes: Cleric","Related Zones: Greater Faydark","Related NPCs: a decaying skeleton","Required Faction: Apprehensive or better"]},"links":["Bone Chips Quests","Felwithe","Yeolarn Bronzeleaf","Cleric","Greater Faydark","A decaying skeleton","Strike","Fine Steel Short Sword","Bone Chips","Clerics of Tunare","King Tearis Thex","Tunare Symbol Quests"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Yeolarn Bronzeleaf","text":"Hail, ______! We of Tunare are charged with protecting the Great Mother from the forces of Innoruuk. Even now, the evil minions of this foul deity are despoiling our great forest. Will you help us [protect the Mother]?"},{"npc":"Yeolarn Bronzeleaf","text":"Just outside the gates of Felwithe, the forces of Innoruuk gather in the guise of decaying skeletons. Bring me four set of bone chips as proof of your vigilance. I assure you, your faith shall not go unrewarded."},{"npc":"Yeolarn Bronzeleaf","text":"Praise Tunare! I knew you would be victorious. I reward you with this spell, and pray that it will help you in your fight against the unholy forces of Innoruuk. When you are ready you will make a fine [Initiate of Tunare]."}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T09:58:34.266Z","outOfEra":false}
